      "post_id": "87550",
      "author_handle": "amanda1212",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 9 years 10 months ago",
      "body": "Hi. I’m expecting my twins very soon. During all pregnancy months I spend my time exercising because I read here that it’s useful to do that. Since I get into exercising I wonder how I could continue exercising with my new born twins. I would like to start jogging, but I’m not sure from where to start. First, I would like to ask if someone of you tried jogging with new-borns?  I know that you need to get a special stroller for it, so I’m wondering about the age that is required for these strollers. I searched a little bit on the internet and found here that there are strollers that a suitable for jogging with twins. I would like to hear your opinion.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10164/#87550",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/91be28b70d116b96fb40.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10164/",
      "role": "original_post",
      "original_post_id": "87550"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "93657",
      "author_handle": "Will_Lily",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 1 year 7 months ago",
      "body": "Having a baby can be tough without family around. Joining some local parenting groups in Paris could really help with support and make you feel more connected.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10164/#93657",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/91be28b70d116b96fb40.html",
