    {
      "post_id": "93786",
      "author_handle": "MollyUK",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 7 months 6 days ago",
      "body": "I love the ambition but with newborns you’ll need to wait a bit before jogging. Most guidance is to wait until around\n6 months\n, when they have strong neck and head control.\nAnd yes, you’ll definitely need a proper jogging stroller designed for twins — the suspension and stability are really important.\nIn the early months, a lot of people stick to walking first (which is still great exercise), then build back up to jogging later.\nAlso worth checking with your doctor before starting again, especially after a twin pregnancy. You’ll get there, just maybe not straight away.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10164/#93786",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/91be28b70d116b96fb40.html",
